WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.633 --> 00:00:01.968
[music playing]

00:00:02.035 --> 00:00:05.605
NARRATOR: Nestling on the east
bank of the Nile, Nefertiti's

00:00:05.672 --> 00:00:09.175
capital city covered
over 3,000 acres,

00:00:09.242 --> 00:00:12.612
and was home to up
to 50,000 people.

00:00:12.679 --> 00:00:16.182
What is now barren landscape
was once one of the greatest

00:00:16.249 --> 00:00:18.618
cities in the ancient world.

00:00:18.685 --> 00:00:21.054
And from these
palaces and temples,

00:00:21.121 --> 00:00:25.959
the royal couple ruled
over all of Egypt.

00:00:26.025 --> 00:00:28.194
She doesn't appear
to be buried here,

00:00:28.261 --> 00:00:31.164
but does this place
hold clues to the fate

00:00:31.231 --> 00:00:32.198
of the missing queen?

00:00:35.635 --> 00:00:37.804
Nefertiti is famous
today because

00:00:37.871 --> 00:00:40.373
of this iconic bust of her.

00:00:40.440 --> 00:00:41.841
She has one of the
most well-known

00:00:41.908 --> 00:00:43.810
faces in all of ancient Egypt.

00:00:48.081 --> 00:00:52.051
This is about the spot that
the bust was actually found.

00:00:52.118 --> 00:00:54.921
We're in the house and the
workshop of a sculptor who was

00:00:54.988 --> 00:00:58.358
probably called Thutmose,
This is where the Nefertiti

00:00:58.425 --> 00:01:01.528
bust was originally created.

00:01:01.594 --> 00:01:04.697
It's one version of
Nefertiti's official portrait.

00:01:04.764 --> 00:01:07.934
She may herself have
signed off on this image.

00:01:08.001 --> 00:01:10.703
But really, we have no idea what
she looked like in real life.

00:01:13.773 --> 00:01:18.344
NARRATOR: Nefertiti's early
life is also still a mystery.

00:01:18.411 --> 00:01:22.115
Her father was probably
Ay, vizier to pharaoh

00:01:22.182 --> 00:01:24.751
Amenhotep III, so
she would have been

00:01:24.818 --> 00:01:27.954
brought up in a royal palace.

00:01:28.021 --> 00:01:30.623
By the age of just
15, she married

00:01:30.690 --> 00:01:35.361
Amenhotep's second son,
the new pharaoh Akhenaten,

00:01:35.428 --> 00:01:38.932
and bore him six daughters.

00:01:38.998 --> 00:01:41.501
As his queen, Nefertiti
became the most

00:01:41.568 --> 00:01:43.670
powerful woman in all of Egypt.

00:01:48.007 --> 00:01:52.378
Yet Nefertiti's ultimate fate
remains a mystery that occupies

00:01:52.445 --> 00:01:54.948
archaeologists all over Egypt.

